@codler Thanks.

I thought `strict` was confusing, since I saw your comment that we can interpret it in either sense. So I propose the `eager` instead of `strict` ( https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/4658/changes/1b4d0b86cc36dda7a56e04930e1e898c0edea859). This obviously executes before the handler with `eager:true`.

What do you think of it?

